{"labs": [{"id": 0, "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn8le03ob09re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Watchful Neighbors Stop Crime<br /><br />Crime in the city was becoming a daily reality for our residents. Before 2010, the number of home and car break-ins had nearly doubled in the metropolitan area. We had feared walking home at night because so many murders and assaults were reported.\nThe whole city wasn't able to be patrolled at once by police. There was only one solution to the fight against crime: community involvement.", "id": 1, "time": "100 ", "image": "engenn8le03ob09re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "In response to the ever-increasing crime rates, neighborhood watch programs sprang up all over the city. What is neighborhood watch? In simple terms, it is a program that is supposed to organize residents to help protect the community.\nPeople who live in the area volunteer to watch out for suspicious occurrences and to exchange information with each other, city officials, and the police force. The result is supposed to be a safer community with a better quality of life.", "id": 2, "time": "25500", "image": "engenn8le03ob09re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "In all six of the districts that began programs, the rate of breaking and entering has decreased to almost zero. In one district, two burglars were caught breaking and entering, and both were arrested, prosecuted, and convicted.\nAs one resident put it, \"I'm glad we had started a neighborhood watch program as early as we did. Neighborhood watch scares off criminals.\"", "id": 3, "time": "53500", "image": "engenn8le03ob09re2img02.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn8le03ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn8le03ob09re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "type": "WLC", "questions":