type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe rules and obligations through a wider range of language and expressions in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple Past Passive", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use an active structure when you want the 'doer' of the action to be the subject.<br /> You use a passive structure when you want the 'receiver' of the action to be the subject. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Active sentence = <span class=\"italic\">People (subject) reported murders (object) in our area.</span><br />Passive sentence = <span class=\"italic\">Murders (subject) <span class=\"strong\">were reported</span> in our area (by people).</span><br /><br/>It is not necessary to mention the object in a passive sentence. <br /><br />  You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of the 'to be' verb followed by the past participle. <br /><br />  The Simple Past passive form is:<br /><br />  was/were + past participle<br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">The building <span class=\"strong\">was built</span> in 1993.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The whole city wasn't patrolled at once by police. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Many murders and assaults were reported.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Past Perfect Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Past Perfect tense to identify and talk about an 'earlier past'.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you are talking about a past event, you can refer to something that happened at an earlier time to that past event by using the Past Perfect tense.<br /><br />  The structure of the Past Perfect is:<br /><br />  Subject + had + past participle <br /><br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">When I arrived at the party, Vanessa <span class=\"strong\">had </span>already<span class=\"strong\"> gone </span>home. </span><br /> Which event happened <span class=\"italic\">first</span>? Vanessa went home.<br /> Which event happened <span class=\"italic\">later</span>? I arrived at the party.<br /><br /> You use the Past Perfect tense (not Simple Past) when you want to talk about how long something had continued <span class=\"strong\">up to a past moment</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Before 2010, the number of home and car break-ins had nearly doubled in the metropolitan area. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We had feared walking home at night.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "\"I'm glad we had started a neighborhood watch program as early as we did.\"", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "watchful ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "observant; attentive", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Watchful neighbors stop crime.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about neighborhood watch.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "break-in", "type": "name"}, {"content": " an occasion when someone illegally enters a building", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Before 2010, the number of home and car break-ins had nearly doubled in the metropolitan area. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to patrol", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to keep watch over (an area) by regularly  traveling around or through it", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The whole city wasn't able to be patrolled at once by police.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to spring up ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to appear suddenly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Neighborhood watch programs sprang up all over the city.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to watch out for", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to look for", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: People who live in the area volunteer to watch out for criminals. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "suspicious", "type": "name"}, {"content": "causing someone to believe that something is not right", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Neighbors look for suspicious activity.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "occurrence", "type": "name"}, {"content": "happening; incident; event ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Neighbors look for suspicious occurrences.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "quality of life", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the standard of health, comfort, and happiness experienced by an individual or group", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The result is supposed to be a safer community with a better quality of life.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob09aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "breaking and entering", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the act of illegally opening and entering someone's house", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In all six of the districts that began programs, the rate of breaking and entering has decreased to almost zero.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob09aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "On the internet, research neighborhood watch and what it does.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Think about your own community and how neighborhood watch could help.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, develop a neighborhood watch program for your community. Write a list of things that neighbors can do to reduce crime.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a poster to advertise your neighborhood watch group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your ideas and your poster to your group.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about rules, regulations, crime and punishment.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about what is supposed to happen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about things that I had done or things that had happened.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I develop and talk about a plan to reduce crime in my community.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}